| `{{ project_name }}-{{ environment }}-running-tasks` | fewer than {{ min_tasks }} task(s) run for 3 minutes, or no task reports metrics | ECS → cluster `{{ project_name }}-{{ environment }}` → service → Events and stopped tasks' "Stopped reason" |
| `{{ project_name }}-{{ environment }}-cpu-high` | average CPU above 85 % for 5 minutes | the task count against `max_tasks` ({{ max_tasks }}); scale-out events |

Express Mode also creates its own alarm that watches each rollout. ECS uses it to roll a bad rollout back. It is not in this list, and it does not notify the topic.

## A rollout that fails

Apply waits for a steady state. If the new image never passes `GET /health`, the apply fails and the earlier image keeps serving. Check the service events, then run the verifier: it reports which digest the tasks run. Terraform state then holds the failed digest. Plan again with the digest that works.

## A task that cannot read its secret

The service events and the stopped task show `ResourceInitializationError: unable to pull secrets or registry auth`, and no log line from the app. The secret has no value, lacks a key that `secret_names` lists, or was deleted. Check it: `aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id {{ project_name }}-{{ environment }}/app --query SecretString` and compare its keys with `secret_names`. Set the value with `put-secret-value`, then `aws ecs update-service --force-new-deployment`.

## Patch the base image

The `Dockerfile` pins `python:3.13-slim` by digest, so security fixes do not arrive on their own. When a new digest ships, update the `FROM` line, run `bash build_image.sh` and deploy the digest it prints. The new `Dockerfile` gives the image a new tag. Python 3.13 reaches end of life in October 2029.
